title The fold line moved, and nothing sank
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Caravan lift arc
think Standfast pass first, run rather than recited: crux/REDS.md clear through %142, era suite GREEN at 12 of 12 before any constructive work.
think Council rota lap index: git log holds 3281 commits, 3281 mod 5 = 1, so row 1 -- Air/Saturn, law and boundary: TAME core, single-stranded, Conway's law.
think Priced word_at: forty-five rungs declare it, all forty-five wrote the same twelve-line body, forty-four fold because confer.rye sits below the fold line.
think Read the body's reaches before lifting. Words is each rung's own list shape so the lift takes the rung for that one name; capabilities.max_caps_per_dependent and std.mem.splitScalar both live in modules the harness already imports.
think Carry fell 65,579 to 65,180 -- exactly the predicted 399, the eighth exact hit.
think Then the sink meter answered 235 where it had answered 247 all arc, and I checked rather than assumed. Nothing sank; confer.rye keeps its word_at body and that body simply stopped being a copy of anything once the forty-four above it folded.
think The copy witness refused my doc block for naming the harness's own parameter in prose. A rung reading its own three-line stub would meet a parameter name that means nothing at that file, which is exactly what the guard is for. Rewrote the line as a reach through the type handed in.
think Declined to book either write-time refusal as a ledger row. Nothing escaped, nothing was claimed, nothing was believed -- the ledger is for what got past a guard, and %142 was booked precisely because that shape stood through three laps.
think The pin roster in the visibility witness had grown one per lap. Slid it to the four most recent lifts and wrote why in the witness itself: the carry ceiling holds the rest, since a returning body raises the carry and the ceiling only comes down.
obs A number falling is not always a thing removed. The fold line's 247 to 235 is the same tree correctly re-read after its neighbors changed, and reading it as a loss would have sent a lap looking for something that had not happened.
obs Conway's law read this morning names exactly why the guards matter here: the organization forgets, so a claim is replaced by a program that re-proves itself. Both refusals this lap came from programs, not from anyone remembering.
obs A witness that accumulates one pin per lap grows without bound. Sliding a fixed window and naming the meter that holds the rest is the bounded form, and it is the same discipline TAME asks of a collection.
